From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:45:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): fold the phone drawer's primary nav into one strip

On a phone, New session, Automations, Inbox and Canvas render as four
44px rows that take about 179px above the session list. At phone width
the drawer now shows them as one strip of equal-width icon-over-label
cells (at least 44px tall) in a rounded glass container, which gives the
session list roughly four more rows. Usage and extension pages add cells
and the strip scrolls sideways, bringing an active cell into view.

Every item now renders through PrimaryNavLink, which takes a row or cell
layout, so both layouts share one definition per destination. The cells
keep their test ids, component ids, links, drawer closing and active
highlight; New keeps the accessible name "New session" and its
aria-keyshortcuts, and the Inbox count sits on the cell's corner with the
same label. Desktop, tablet and the side-by-side layout on wide phones
keep the stacked rows.

Refs #13482

[Desidero: Automations stays unconditional (this base has no
automations_enabled gate), and New session keeps the project prompt's click
handler from new-chat-project-prompt]

Not upstream yet: proposed from feat/mobile-sidebar-nav-strip; drop this copy once it merges.

Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit ab6877bc3454e3b0ae0121f453a51c96a02e3450)
